It uses an optimized approach with two pointers:
1. Iterate through each element as the first number of the triplet.
2. For each first number, use two pointers (one at next index and one at end) to find the other two numbers that sum to the negative of the first number.
3. Skips duplicates to avoid checking the same triplet multiple times.

This implementation has O(n^2) time complexity and O(1) space complexity.

